Looking at the grid, each triangle in the grid contains exactly one single‑outline star and two double (nested) stars. Examining the edges around the missing (downward‑pointing) triangle: the star on its left edge (shared with the triangle to its left) is a single star, while the stars at its other two vertices (top‑right and bottom) are double stars, as seen in the neighboring triangles. This matches the option where the single star is at the top‑left position and the other two stars are double‑outlined.

This corresponds to the option with a single star at the top‑left and double stars elsewhere, i.e., option B.

